      "tex_lines": {
        "286": "For $f\\ge 1$, define $q_{-}=\\lfloor\\frac{f}{2}\\rfloor$ and $q^{+}=\\lceil\\frac{f}{2}\\rceil$;",
        "294": "and for $d\\geq f$, blocks of length $2f$ will be defined,",
        "295": "for every $k\\geq 1$ by:",
        "300": "$\\LL_f(d)=k(f+1+q_{-})+q^{+}+1-j\\cdot (k-1)$, if $d=(2k-1)f+q^{+}+1+j$ for $0\\leq j\\leq q_{-}+1$;",
        "301": "\\item[] with the correction that, if $f\\leq 4$ or $k>1$ then $k$ ",
        "302": "is to be subtracted from $\\LL_f(2kf-1)$;",
        "338": "\\item[] $\\LL_4(5)=2$;",
        "339": "\\item[] $\\LL_4(36)=5$;",
        "340": "\\item[] add $\\frac{d+44}{8}$ to $\\LL_4(d)$ for $d\\equiv 4\\bmod 8$ ",
        "341": "with $d\\geq 44$.",
        "403": "\\begin{conjecture}\\label{conj:per}",
        "404": "For all $f, d=g-f\\geq 1$ the strict, greedy 2-sum sequence",
        "405": "$S_{f,g}$ is ultimately periodic with length of the period $\\PP(d,f)=\\LL_f(d)$."
      }
    },
